  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I have bulk RNA-seq from mouse cortex at five developmental stages (E14, E17, P0, P7, adult), eight animals per stage, 40 samples in total, together with a TF-to-gene motif prior and a TF-TF interaction table. I want an estimate of how active each transcription factor is in each sample, so I can plot TF activity by stage. Signed effects of each TF on its targets would be a bonus."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want an estimate of how active each transcription factor is in each sample, so I can plot TF activity by stage.\" -- available from GIRAFFE.\n2. \"Signed effects of each TF on its targets would be a bonus.\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n\n**GIRAFFE**. GIRAFFE jointly factors expression into a regulatory-effect matrix and sample-varying TF activities using biological priors. Signed effects describe the fitted activation/repression relationship, while activity differs from the TF's own expression. These fitted coefficients do not alone establish causality.\n\nYou would need expression matrix, motif/prior, PPI network. The analysis would provide inferred regulator-to-target associations; inferred transcription-factor-by-sample activity values.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
